  "body": "Combines and squashes the two earlier PRs (#20 scanner code + #21 Grimoire/consolidation) into one self-contained change.\n\n## CODE \u2014 multi-language scanner (NECROMANCY `language_agnostic`)\n- **`mantle/assimilator/scanner_ts.py`** \u2014 tree-sitter parser surface for `.js/.mjs/.go/.rs`, emitting the same `{symbol, kind, line, role}` records as the Python scanner, reusing `classify_symbol` unchanged.\n- **`scanner.py`** \u2014 `scan_project` routes those extensions through `scanner_ts` when the optional tree-sitter stack is installed; falls back to Python-only otherwise (no behavior change for existing users).\n- **`examples/sample_app/notes_app.js`** + **`examples/tests/test_multilang_parity.py`** \u2014 assert the JS organ map equals the Python organ map and the scan is read-only; skip cleanly without tree-sitter.\n- **`pyproject.toml`** \u2014 optional `multilang` extra (`pip install mantle-os[multilang]`).\n\n## DOCS \u2014 the Grimoire, AppAI chapter as the single source of truth\n- **`docs/grimoire/`** \u2014 `THE_GRIMOIRE_CORE_v3_0.md` + `GRIMOIRE_APPAI_DOMAIN_v1_0.md` + index README.\n- The AppAI chapter gains **\"NECROMANCY \u2014 operational detail\"** (prime directive, Phase-0 gate, 17-phase pipeline, role table, hook runtime, hard-fails, APP_INVENTORY template) and a **\"One substrate, two casts\"** note unifying egg/RESURGERE with assimilation/NECROMANCY. `language_agnostic` updated proposed \u2192 **shipped**.\n- **`Mantle_Assimilator.md`** and **`docs/v3/Assimilation_Guide.md`** reduced to pointer stubs; `README`, `Mantle_PRIMER`, `Mantle_v3_Architecture`, `Mantle_Organism_Lens` repointed to the canonical chapter.\n- Doctrine-of-record cross-ref comments in `scanner.py`, `anchor.py`, `graft.py`, `vault.py` (comments only).\n\n## Why one PR\nThe docs reference the shipped `scanner_ts.py` and the code implements the doctrine the chapter describes \u2014 they're one feature. Squashed to a single commit so the reference always resolves.\n\n## Note: the code was already single-source\n`mantle/assimilator/scanner.py` is the only scanner/classifier; `anchor.py`, `graft.py`, and the egg/RESURGERE path (`vault.py` \u2192 `hatchery.incubate`) all reuse it. This PR makes the docs match that reality.\n\n## Test plan\n- [x] `python -m mantle audit` \u2014 Stage-1 gate passes\n- [x] `python -m mantle prove` \u2014 68/68 invariants green\n- [x] `python -m mantle assimilate examples/sample_app --dry-run` \u2014 read-only (0 host files modified)\n- [x] `python -m unittest examples.tests.test_multilang_parity` \u2014 OK (tree-sitter cases skip without the extra)\n- [x] doctor docs-vs-code coherence check green\n- [ ] CI / maintainer: run the parity test with `pip install mantle-os[multilang]` (tree-sitter 0.21.x needs Python <3.12) to exercise the tree-sitter path end-to-end\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
